Chapter: E1000RxInvisible
  cites Foreword chapter Maybe
  cites Kernel chapter E1000e
  cites Kernel chapter Pci

 The row sitting 9 read off the ASUS on 2026-08-21 and that this bed could not
 produce: the MAC counts a frame in GPRC, RNBC stays 0, and no descriptor is
 written back, so the ring the driver is reading shows nothing. DiagNicRing
 calls it "frames arrived and we cannot see them" (:124). It sits between
 "nothing arrived" (:122) and "turned away for want of a descriptor" (:127),
 and a driver acts on the three differently, which is why the counters are
 read together and never the ring alone.

 codex-vm counted GPRC inside the delivery loop just after DD was written, so
 all three ways of stopping a receive returned above it and every one of them
 read gprc=0: the bed could only ever answer the row ABOVE this one, whatever
 fault it was given. Counting where the MAC accepts the frame is the fix, and
 it took no new switch.

 BUS MASTER CLEAR IS THE CAUSE THIS ARM USES, and the choice is forced rather
 than preferred. The K1 stall is the cause sitting 9 read, but the canned
 injector delivers its whole budget at the RCTL.EN write, and e1000-init has
 performed the shipped K1 step by then, so nothing on this path can be stalled
 at the moment frames arrive. BME is clear from before bring-up, so it reaches
 the same row without the sequencing. The K1 half of the same fix rides the
 NAT path, where frames arrive over time, and belongs to the diag image's
 nicring stage rather than here.

 e1000-rx-invisible-off is this arm with bus mastering left alone. Neither
 means anything alone: gprc>0 is NOT the discriminator, because the control
 reads gprc>0 too. The pair differs on the received frame, and that is the
 whole reading.

Section: Fixtures

  bring-up : PciScanResult -> E1000Device
  bring-up (scan) =
    when e1000-find scan
      is Just (d) -> e1000-init d
      is None -> e1000-absent

Section: Judges

  yn : Boolean -> Text
  yn (b) = if b then "yes" else "no"

  over-zero : Integer -> Text
  over-zero (n) = if n > 0 then "yes" else "no"

Section: Entry

  opening : [Console] Nothing = act
    let d = bring-up (pci-scan-bus 0)
    in let r = e1000-poll-frame d
    in let gprc = e1000-read (d.e-mmio) e1000-reg-gprc
    in let rnbc = e1000-read (d.e-mmio) e1000-reg-rnbc
    in act
      print-line-uni ("present       : " & yn (d.e-present))
      print-line-uni ("link up       : " & yn (e1000-has-link d))
      print-line-uni ("recv happened : " & yn (r.r-has-frame))
      print-line-uni ("gprc over 0   : " & over-zero gprc)
      print-line-uni ("rnbc over 0   : " & over-zero rnbc)
    end
  end
